From d9372e61263c4ebd6b5196504a3c963c28cda44e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 10:07:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 180/180] patch 0180 -- phase-tagged gameplay-IO-audit hook
 (v1.0.3 clean re-author)

Clean re-author of the SFXPAUSE-013 IO-audit hook -- the permanent
lazy-IO landmine detector that powers the no-gameplay-IO dev gate.
Every instrumented filesystem-IO entry point emits its current game
phase (boot / load_stage / gameplay), so a DOSBox-X run maps each IO
op to WHEN it happens. phase=gameplay IO = a latent real-HW stall
(the actionable subset).

Env SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_IO_AUDIT=1 (cached strict-truthy, default OFF).
Emit: [io-audit] phase=NAME op=OPTYPE file=BASENAME bytes=N wall_us=N.
3-state phase enum driven by an RAII guard in load_stage (sets
load_stage on entry, restores gameplay on all return paths;
boot -> gameplay implicit on the first load_stage dtor).

6 instrumented sites (op tag): Surface::loadImage (loadImage; the
SFXPAUSE-012 sprite-sheet case + any lazy surface), TSC::Load
(tsc_load), Organya::load (music_org_load), Ogg::load
(music_ogg_load), profile_load / profile_save (save_read /
save_write). loadImage + profile use local RAII guards covering all
return paths; tsc/Organya/Ogg use inline brackets.

Central infra (io_audit_enabled / io_audit_set_phase /
io_audit_get_phase / io_audit_emit) in main.cpp, extern "C" so the
consumer TUs link without header churn. io_audit_emit strips the path
to basename via SDL_strrchr.

Self-contained -- no dependency on the patch-0175 cave counter (tags
phase, not cave). Validates the 0178 fix: with both
EAGER_SHEET_RELOAD off + SKIP_SHEET_FLUSH default-ON, sprite
loadImage ops appear ONLY at cave-1 first-visit, never recurring at
phase=gameplay. Default OFF -> production byte-identical to golden.

Workspace-local; never upstreamed.
